<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mariana Islands</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Marianas</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mariana Islands are a chain of fifteen volcanic islands in the western Pacific, including Guam, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saipan">Saipan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tinian">Tinian</a> and Rota. Settled by the ancestors of the Chamorro about 3,500 years ago, they were colonised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> from 1668. After 1898 Guam went to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and the rest to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>; since 1978 the northern islands have formed a US commonwealth.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mariana-islands.jpg" alt="Mariana Islands" width="320" height="487" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wikid77 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_Mariana_Islands_volcanoes.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
